WrapperToken::unwrap
├── given contract is paused
│   └── it should revert with IsPaused
└── given contract is not paused
    ├── when user has insufficient wrapped token balance
    │   └── it should revert
    ├── when previewUnwrap returns zero
    │   ├── when wrappedTokenAmount is zero
    │   │   └── it should revert with InvalidInput
    │   └── when computed pt amount rounds down to zero
    │       └── it should revert with InvalidInput
    └── when previewUnwrap returns greater than zero
        ├── it should burn wrapped tokens from caller
        ├── it should transfer previewUnwrap amount to caller
        ├── it should reduce wrapper underlying token balance by previewUnwrap amount
        ├── it should emit Unwrapped
        ├── it should return previewUnwrap amount
        ├── given exchangeRate equals 10 ** DECIMALS
        │   └── it should transfer PT to caller one-to-one with wrapped amount
        └── given exchangeRate is not 10 ** DECIMALS
            ├── given exchangeRate is greater than 10 ** DECIMALS
            │   ├── it should transfer rounded-down PT amount
            │   └── when wrappedTokenAmount times exchangeRate divides evenly by 10 ** DECIMALS
            │       └── it should transfer exact PT amount without rounding loss
            ├── given exchangeRate is less than 10 ** DECIMALS
            │   └── it should return fewer PT per wrapped token than one-to-one when not exact
            └── when caller unwraps wrapped tokens minted from a prior wrap at same exchangeRate
                └── it should not guarantee recovering the original ptAmount due to asymmetric rounding
